---
// Article for the Small Text page. The tool above it comes from SmallPage.
import SmallPage from '../components/SmallPage.astro';
---

<SmallPage lang="en">
  <article class="wrap max-w-[900px] mx-auto py-10 text-text">
    <!-- Styles -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold">Copy-and-paste Tiny Text Styles</h2>
      <p class="mb-5 leading-[1.8] text-text-muted">Small text also appear as tiny text, or tiny fonts. Also your social media bios, usernames and messages to uniquely stand out, these typing style are called Superscript, Small Caps, and Subscript.</p>
      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="group rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5 transition hover:border-primary hover:-translate-y-0.5">
          <span class="inline-block rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-primary">SS</span>
          <p class="mt-3 text-3xl leading-tight" dir="ltr">ᵗⁱⁿʸ</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-base font-semibold">Superscript</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-text-muted leading-[1.6]">Raised tiny letters that sit above the line.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="group rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5 transition hover:border-primary hover:-translate-y-0.5">
          <span class="inline-block rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-primary">SC</span>
          <p class="mt-3 text-3xl leading-tight" dir="ltr">ᴛɪɴʏ</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-base font-semibold">Small Caps</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-text-muted leading-[1.6]">Miniature capitals at lowercase height.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="group rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5 transition hover:border-primary hover:-translate-y-0.5">
          <span class="inline-block rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-semibold text-primary">SB</span>
          <p class="mt-3 text-3xl leading-tight" dir="ltr">ₜᵢₙy</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-base font-semibold">Subscript</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-text-muted leading-[1.6]">Lowered tiny letters that sit below the line.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How to -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-bold">How to use Tiny Text Generator</h2>
      <ol class="m-0 flex list-none flex-col gap-3 p-0">
        <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-4">
          <span class="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary text-sm font-bold text-white">1</span>
          <p class="m-0 text-[.95rem] leading-[1.7]"><strong class="font-semibold">Type your text.</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Enter your name, bio, or any phrase into the box above to shrink your letters instantly.</span></p>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-4">
          <span class="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary text-sm font-bold text-white">2</span>
          <p class="m-0 text-[.95rem] leading-[1.7]"><strong class="font-semibold">Pick a tiny style.</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Choose between superscript (ᵗⁱⁿʸ), subscript (ₜᵢₙy), or small caps (ᴛɪɴʏ) to find the right miniature look.</span></p>
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-4">
          <span class="flex h-9 w-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary text-sm font-bold text-white">3</span>
          <p class="m-0 text-[.95rem] leading-[1.7]"><strong class="font-semibold">Copy and paste.</strong> <span class="text-text-muted">Click your favorite small text style to copy it.</span></p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Alphabets -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold">Small Text Letters Alphabets</h2>
      <p class="mb-5 leading-[1.8] text-text-muted">In order to copy these use SS, SC, and SB respectively as shown in example below:</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><span class="rounded-md bg-primary px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-white">SS</span><h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Superscript (raised tiny letters)</h3></div>
        <p class="text-2xl leading-[1.9] break-words select-all tracking-wide" dir="ltr">ᵃ ᵇ ᶜ ᵈ ᵉ ᶠ ᵍ ʰ ⁱ ʲ ᵏ ˡ ᵐ ⁿ ᵒ ᵖ q ʳ ˢ ᵗ ᵘ ᵛ ʷ ˣ ʸ ᶻ</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><span class="rounded-md bg-primary px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-white">SC</span><h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Small caps (miniature capitals)</h3></div>
        <p class="text-2xl leading-[1.9] break-words select-all tracking-wide" dir="ltr">ᴀ ʙ ᴄ ᴅ ᴇ ꜰ ɢ ʜ ɪ ᴊ ᴋ ʟ ᴍ ɴ ᴏ ᴘ ǫ ʀ s ᴛ ᴜ ᴠ ᴡ x ʏ ᴢ</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><span class="rounded-md bg-primary px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-white">SB</span><h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Subscript (lowered tiny letters)</h3></div>
        <p class="text-2xl leading-[1.9] break-words select-all tracking-wide" dir="ltr">ₐ ₑ ₕ ᵢ ⱼ ₖ ₗ ₘ ₙ ₒ ₚ ᵣ ₛ ₜ ᵤ ᵥ ₓ</p>
        <p class="mt-3 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-primary bg-surface-2 px-3 py-2 text-sm leading-[1.6] text-text-muted"><strong class="text-text">Note:</strong> Standard Unicode does not include native subscript letters for b, c, d, f, g, q, w, and z.</p>
      </div>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><span class="rounded-md bg-primary px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-white">SS</span><h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Superscript Numbers</h3></div>
        <p class="text-2xl leading-[1.9] break-words select-all tracking-wide" dir="ltr">⁰ ¹ ² ³ ⁴ ⁵ ⁶ ⁷ ⁸ ⁹</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-5">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><span class="rounded-md bg-primary px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-white">SB</span><h3 class="text-base font-semibold">Subscript Numbers</h3></div>
        <p class="text-2xl leading-[1.9] break-words select-all tracking-wide" dir="ltr">₀ ₁ ₂ ₃ ₄ ₅ ₆ ₇ ₈ ₉</p>
      </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-5 text-center text-2xl font-bold">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-[720px] flex-col gap-3">
      <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface px-5 py-4">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-[.95rem] font-medium">
          Is this small font usable on Facebook, Twitter, Tumblr and YouTube?
          <span class="shrink-0 text-text-muted transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[.9rem] leading-[1.7] text-text-muted">Yes, you can easily use this small letters on Facebook, Twitter (X), Tumblr, and YouTube because it is made of universal Unicode symbols.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface px-5 py-4">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-[.95rem] font-medium">
          Can I use tiny letters in my Instagram username?
          <span class="shrink-0 text-text-muted transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[.9rem] leading-[1.7] text-text-muted">Instagram handles only allow standard letters, numbers, periods, and underscores, so Unicode symbols won't work there. However, you can freely use them in your Instagram Name field, Bio, and Captions.</p>
      </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</SmallPage>
